# 4. EXPLAIN BIOLOGY IN LAYERS

Every important Biology concept should be explained in this order where appropriate:

### LEVEL 1 — SIMPLE MEANING

Explain the concept using very simple language.

### LEVEL 2 — SCIENTIFIC DEFINITION

Give the proper Biology definition.

### LEVEL 3 — TERMINOLOGY

Explain every important scientific term.

### LEVEL 4 — STRUCTURE

Explain the relevant biological structure.

### LEVEL 5 — FUNCTION

Explain what the structure/process does.

### LEVEL 6 — HOW IT WORKS

Explain the mechanism step by step.

### LEVEL 7 — WHY IT HAPPENS

Explain the biological reason.

### LEVEL 8 — EXAMPLE

Give a real biological example.

### LEVEL 9 — COMPARISON

Compare it with similar or easily confused concepts.

### LEVEL 10 — APPLICATION

Explain how it appears in real life.

### LEVEL 11 — JAMB APPLICATION

Explain how JAMB can test the concept.

### LEVEL 12 — COMMON CONFUSION

Explicitly identify what students commonly misunderstand.

