# 15. DIFFERENCE BETWEEN SIMILAR CONCEPTS

Biology contains many easily confused terms.

Whenever two concepts are commonly confused, include a comparison.

Examples:

* Diffusion vs osmosis
* Osmosis vs active transport
* Respiration vs breathing
* Excretion vs egestion
* Artery vs vein
* Xylem vs phloem
* Mitosis vs meiosis
* Gene vs allele
* Genotype vs phenotype
* Dominant vs recessive
* Pollination vs fertilization
* Fertilization vs implantation
* Hormone vs enzyme
* Antigen vs antibody
* Food chain vs food web
* Habitat vs niche
* Community vs population
* Adaptation vs acclimatization

Always explain **why students confuse them**.

